{
  "total": 770.422,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "S01",
      "start": 0.4,
      "speech_end": 8.05,
      "end": 8.85,
      "dur": 8.45,
      "text": "Microsoft has the source code to Windows. They wrote the APIs. They know exactly how it works inside."
    },
    {
      "id": "S02",
      "start": 8.85,
      "speech_end": 14.35,
      "end": 15.15,
      "dur": 6.3,
      "text": "They have had thirty years, and some of the largest engineering teams in the history of software."
    },
    {
      "id": "S03",
      "start": 15.15,
      "speech_end": 16.409,
      "end": 17.809,
      "dur": 2.659,
      "text": "And yet."
    },
    {
      "id": "S04",
      "start": 17.809,
      "speech_end": 21.619,
      "end": 22.419,
      "dur": 4.61,
      "text": "Watch what a serious Windows user does on a brand new machine."
    },
    {
      "id": "S05",
      "start": 22.419,
      "speech_end": 28.823,
      "end": 29.623,
      "dur": 7.204,
      "text": "They install a different file manager. A different search tool. A different archive program."
    },
    {
      "id": "S05b",
      "start": 29.623,
      "speech_end": 32.332,
      "end": 33.132,
      "dur": 3.509,
      "text": "Image viewer. Video player. Music player."
    },
    {
      "id": "S05c",
      "start": 33.132,
      "speech_end": 35.872,
      "end": 36.672,
      "dur": 3.54,
      "text": "PDF reader. Text editor."
    },
    {
      "id": "S05d",
      "start": 36.672,
      "speech_end": 38.232,
      "end": 39.032,
      "dur": 2.36,
      "text": "And the list goes on..."
    },
    {
      "id": "S06",
      "start": 39.032,
      "speech_end": 42.342,
      "end": 43.142,
      "dur": 4.11,
      "text": "Before they do any actual work, they rebuild the toolbox."
    },
    {
      "id": "S07",
      "start": 43.142,
      "speech_end": 49.502,
      "end": 52.302,
      "dur": 9.16,
      "text": "So here is the question. Why doesn't Windows come with the tools you need the moment the work gets harder?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S08",
      "start": 52.302,
      "speech_end": 54.132,
      "end": 54.932,
      "dur": 2.63,
      "text": "Start with the file manager."
    },
    {
      "id": "S09",
      "start": 54.932,
      "speech_end": 60.292,
      "end": 61.092,
      "dur": 6.16,
      "text": "If you only want to open a folder and double-click a document, File Explorer is fine."
    },
    {
      "id": "S10",
      "start": 61.092,
      "speech_end": 63.522,
      "end": 64.322,
      "dur": 3.23,
      "text": "But if you need to do more with files..."
    },
    {
      "id": "S11",
      "start": 64.322,
      "speech_end": 73.212,
      "end": 74.012,
      "dur": 9.69,
      "text": "Compare two folders and sync them. Rename three hundred files by a pattern. See folder sizes without opening each one."
    },
    {
      "id": "S12",
      "start": 74.012,
      "speech_end": 78.257,
      "end": 79.057,
      "dur": 5.045,
      "text": "And you discover a program that has been doing all of that since 1993."
    },
    {
      "id": "S13",
      "start": 79.057,
      "speech_end": 83.431,
      "end": 84.231,
      "dur": 5.173,
      "text": "Two panels. Keyboard shortcuts. Synchronise. Compare. Rename. Archive."
    },
    {
      "id": "S14",
      "start": 84.231,
      "speech_end": 88.369,
      "end": 89.169,
      "dur": 4.939,
      "text": "Written by one developer. In Switzerland. Called Christian Ghisler."
    },
    {
      "id": "S15",
      "start": 89.169,
      "speech_end": 92.179,
      "end": 92.979,
      "dur": 3.81,
      "text": "And here is the part that says more than the feature list."
    },
    {
      "id": "S16",
      "start": 92.979,
      "speech_end": 96.539,
      "end": 97.339,
      "dur": 4.36,
      "text": "For the first nine years, it was not called Total Commander."
    },
    {
      "id": "S17",
      "start": 97.339,
      "speech_end": 99.299,
      "end": 100.099,
      "dur": 2.76,
      "text": "It was called Windows Commander."
    },
    {
      "id": "S18",
      "start": 100.099,
      "speech_end": 105.109,
      "end": 105.909,
      "dur": 5.81,
      "text": "Then in the summer of 2002, a letter arrived from a firm of lawyers."
    },
    {
      "id": "S19",
      "start": 105.909,
      "speech_end": 110.219,
      "end": 111.019,
      "dur": 5.11,
      "text": "They represented, in their own words, the owner of the trademark Windows."
    },
    {
      "id": "S20",
      "start": 111.019,
      "speech_end": 116.259,
      "end": 118.659,
      "dur": 7.64,
      "text": "So Microsoft did not build that tool. Microsoft made it change its name."
    },
    {
      "id": "S21",
      "start": 118.659,
      "speech_end": 125.029,
      "end": 125.829,
      "dur": 7.17,
      "text": "And before you decide that nobody in Redmond ever had the idea of a proper two-panel file manager..."
    },
    {
      "id": "S22",
      "start": 125.829,
      "speech_end": 127.749,
      "end": 128.549,
      "dur": 2.72,
      "text": "They did have it. They shipped it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S23",
      "start": 128.549,
      "speech_end": 133.501,
      "end": 134.301,
      "dur": 5.751,
      "text": "DOS Shell, 1988. Left panel, right panel. In the box."
    },
    {
      "id": "S24",
      "start": 134.301,
      "speech_end": 135.981,
      "end": 138.581,
      "dur": 4.28,
      "text": "Microsoft removed it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S25",
      "start": 138.581,
      "speech_end": 143.821,
      "end": 144.621,
      "dur": 6.04,
      "text": "So the question sharpens immediately. This isn't a gap nobody noticed."
    },
    {
      "id": "S25b",
      "start": 144.621,
      "speech_end": 150.311,
      "end": 151.511,
      "dur": 6.89,
      "text": "By the way, if you like videos like this, consider subscribing. It really helps the channel."
    },
    {
      "id": "S26",
      "start": 151.511,
      "speech_end": 154.001,
      "end": 154.801,
      "dur": 3.29,
      "text": "Keep going, because the pattern repeats."
    },
    {
      "id": "S27",
      "start": 154.801,
      "speech_end": 155.961,
      "end": 156.761,
      "dur": 1.96,
      "text": "Finding a file."
    },
    {
      "id": "S28",
      "start": 156.761,
      "speech_end": 160.951,
      "end": 161.751,
      "dur": 4.99,
      "text": "For years, the reliable answer was a tiny program called Everything."
    },
    {
      "id": "S29",
      "start": 161.751,
      "speech_end": 165.121,
      "end": 165.921,
      "dur": 4.17,
      "text": "You type three letters. The results are already there."
    },
    {
      "id": "S30",
      "start": 165.921,
      "speech_end": 170.781,
      "end": 171.581,
      "dur": 5.66,
      "text": "No waiting. No wondering whether the index has got round to your folder yet."
    },
    {
      "id": "S31",
      "start": 171.581,
      "speech_end": 175.371,
      "end": 176.171,
      "dur": 4.59,
      "text": "And this one deserves a fair hearing, because the trick is not magic."
    },
    {
      "id": "S32",
      "start": 176.171,
      "speech_end": 181.568,
      "end": 182.368,
      "dur": 6.197,
      "text": "On an NTFS drive there is a master file table, a list of everything on the disk."
    },
    {
      "id": "S33",
      "start": 182.368,
      "speech_end": 188.058,
      "end": 188.858,
      "dur": 6.49,
      "text": "Everything reads that list once, then follows the change journal the filesystem is already keeping."
    },
    {
      "id": "S34",
      "start": 188.858,
      "speech_end": 190.948,
      "end": 191.748,
      "dur": 2.89,
      "text": "That is why it feels instant."
    },
    {
      "id": "S35",
      "start": 191.748,
      "speech_end": 195.258,
      "end": 196.058,
      "dur": 4.31,
      "text": "Windows Search is slower because it is doing a harder job."
    },
    {
      "id": "S36",
      "start": 196.058,
      "speech_end": 200.428,
      "end": 201.228,
      "dur": 5.17,
      "text": "It reads inside your documents, and it respects who is allowed to see which file."
    },
    {
      "id": "S37",
      "start": 201.228,
      "speech_end": 205.818,
      "end": 206.618,
      "dur": 5.39,
      "text": "So that one is not a failure. It's a different question being answered."
    },
    {
      "id": "S38",
      "start": 206.618,
      "speech_end": 209.378,
      "end": 211.778,
      "dur": 5.16,
      "text": "Hold on to that, because it is the exception."
    },
    {
      "id": "S39",
      "start": 211.778,
      "speech_end": 213.518,
      "end": 214.318,
      "dur": 2.54,
      "text": "Where did the disk space go?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S40",
      "start": 214.318,
      "speech_end": 217.518,
      "end": 218.318,
      "dur": 4.0,
      "text": "Windows tells you that you have used nine hundred gigabytes."
    },
    {
      "id": "S41",
      "start": 218.318,
      "speech_end": 219.15,
      "end": 219.95,
      "dur": 1.632,
      "text": "Where?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S42",
      "start": 219.95,
      "speech_end": 223.23,
      "end": 224.03,
      "dur": 4.08,
      "text": "And you end up installing a program that draws you a map."
    },
    {
      "id": "S43",
      "start": 224.03,
      "speech_end": 225.91,
      "end": 226.71,
      "dur": 2.68,
      "text": "And what about copying files?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S44",
      "start": 226.71,
      "speech_end": 230.98,
      "end": 231.78,
      "dur": 5.07,
      "text": "Historically, if one file failed, Explorer cancelled the whole copy."
    },
    {
      "id": "S45",
      "start": 231.78,
      "speech_end": 233.12,
      "end": 233.92,
      "dur": 2.14,
      "text": "Which files made it?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S45b",
      "start": 233.92,
      "speech_end": 237.11,
      "end": 237.91,
      "dur": 3.99,
      "text": "Where do I pick it up? Can I skip just that one?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S46",
      "start": 237.91,
      "speech_end": 242.8,
      "end": 243.6,
      "dur": 5.69,
      "text": "So people installed something that would skip it, carry on, and tell them what it skipped."
    },
    {
      "id": "S46b",
      "start": 243.6,
      "speech_end": 248.49,
      "end": 249.29,
      "dur": 5.69,
      "text": "Deleting has a different mystery. That one has a whole video of its own."
    },
    {
      "id": "S47",
      "start": 249.29,
      "speech_end": 253.025,
      "end": 253.825,
      "dur": 4.535,
      "text": "What about archives? Windows opens a zip file."
    },
    {
      "id": "S48",
      "start": 253.825,
      "speech_end": 257.015,
      "end": 257.815,
      "dur": 3.99,
      "text": "But there is a difference between supporting a format..."
    },
    {
      "id": "S49",
      "start": 257.815,
      "speech_end": 260.095,
      "end": 260.895,
      "dur": 3.08,
      "text": "...and giving someone a good tool for it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S50",
      "start": 260.895,
      "speech_end": 264.405,
      "end": 265.205,
      "dur": 4.31,
      "text": "Screenshots. Print screen, open Paint, paste, crop."
    },
    {
      "id": "S51",
      "start": 265.205,
      "speech_end": 267.815,
      "end": 268.615,
      "dur": 3.41,
      "text": "You had to do that for about twenty years."
    },
    {
      "id": "S52",
      "start": 268.615,
      "speech_end": 272.525,
      "end": 273.325,
      "dur": 4.71,
      "text": "And uninstalling software is where it gets genuinely strange."
    },
    {
      "id": "S53",
      "start": 273.325,
      "speech_end": 279.745,
      "end": 280.545,
      "dur": 7.22,
      "text": "Programs left files behind. Registry entries. Folders nobody would ever find."
    },
    {
      "id": "S54",
      "start": 280.545,
      "speech_end": 283.212,
      "end": 284.012,
      "dur": 3.467,
      "text": "So people installed better uninstallers."
    },
    {
      "id": "S55",
      "start": 284.012,
      "speech_end": 287.772,
      "end": 288.572,
      "dur": 4.56,
      "text": "But some of those uninstallers had a stranger job than that."
    },
    {
      "id": "S56",
      "start": 288.572,
      "speech_end": 289.916,
      "end": 290.716,
      "dur": 2.144,
      "text": "They watched."
    },
    {
      "id": "S57",
      "start": 290.716,
      "speech_end": 295.176,
      "end": 295.976,
      "dur": 5.26,
      "text": "You ran them first, then you ran the installer, and they recorded what changed."
    },
    {
      "id": "S58",
      "start": 295.976,
      "speech_end": 297.566,
      "end": 298.966,
      "dur": 2.99,
      "text": "Think about what that means."
    },
    {
      "id": "S59",
      "start": 298.966,
      "speech_end": 302.926,
      "end": 303.726,
      "dur": 4.76,
      "text": "You installed a program to watch another program install itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "S60",
      "start": 303.726,
      "speech_end": 306.786,
      "end": 309.586,
      "dur": 5.86,
      "text": "Because Windows itself did not necessarily know."
    },
    {
      "id": "S61",
      "start": 309.586,
      "speech_end": 311.916,
      "end": 312.716,
      "dur": 3.13,
      "text": "Which brings us to the sharpest case."
    },
    {
      "id": "S62",
      "start": 312.716,
      "speech_end": 313.806,
      "end": 314.606,
      "dur": 1.89,
      "text": "Not responding."
    },
    {
      "id": "S63",
      "start": 314.606,
      "speech_end": 317.496,
      "end": 318.296,
      "dur": 3.69,
      "text": "Task Manager knows. It says so on the screen."
    },
    {
      "id": "S64",
      "start": 318.296,
      "speech_end": 321.376,
      "end": 322.176,
      "dur": 3.88,
      "text": "But if you want to know why, you install Process Explorer."
    },
    {
      "id": "S65",
      "start": 322.176,
      "speech_end": 323.05,
      "end": 323.5,
      "dur": 1.325,
      "text": "Threads."
    },
    {
      "id": "S65b",
      "start": 323.5,
      "speech_end": 324.46,
      "end": 324.91,
      "dur": 1.41,
      "text": "Handles."
    },
    {
      "id": "S65c",
      "start": 324.91,
      "speech_end": 329.29,
      "end": 330.09,
      "dur": 5.18,
      "text": "Which file the program is waiting on. Which process started it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S66",
      "start": 330.09,
      "speech_end": 333.653,
      "end": 334.453,
      "dur": 4.363,
      "text": "And Process Explorer came from a company called Sysinternals."
    },
    {
      "id": "S67",
      "start": 334.453,
      "speech_end": 335.943,
      "end": 336.743,
      "dur": 2.29,
      "text": "Microsoft bought them."
    },
    {
      "id": "S68",
      "start": 336.743,
      "speech_end": 338.631,
      "end": 339.431,
      "dur": 2.688,
      "text": "That was in 2006."
    },
    {
      "id": "S69",
      "start": 339.431,
      "speech_end": 341.391,
      "end": 342.191,
      "dur": 2.76,
      "text": "And they got the man who wrote it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S69b",
      "start": 342.191,
      "speech_end": 346.381,
      "end": 347.181,
      "dur": 4.99,
      "text": "Mark Russinovich. Today, he is the CTO of Azure."
    },
    {
      "id": "S70",
      "start": 347.181,
      "speech_end": 351.591,
      "end": 352.391,
      "dur": 5.21,
      "text": "Microsoft has owned that tool, and the person who wrote it, for twenty years."
    },
    {
      "id": "S71",
      "start": 352.391,
      "speech_end": 354.631,
      "end": 355.431,
      "dur": 3.04,
      "text": "They host the download themselves."
    },
    {
      "id": "S72",
      "start": 355.431,
      "speech_end": 357.441,
      "end": 360.241,
      "dur": 4.81,
      "text": "And it is still not in Windows."
    },
    {
      "id": "S73",
      "start": 360.241,
      "speech_end": 363.051,
      "end": 363.851,
      "dur": 3.61,
      "text": "So the answer cannot be that Microsoft couldn't."
    },
    {
      "id": "S74",
      "start": 363.851,
      "speech_end": 367.191,
      "end": 367.991,
      "dur": 4.14,
      "text": "Which means the real question was never why they failed."
    },
    {
      "id": "S75",
      "start": 367.991,
      "speech_end": 369.771,
      "end": 372.771,
      "dur": 4.78,
      "text": "It's why they chose not to."
    },
    {
      "id": "S76",
      "start": 372.771,
      "speech_end": 374.423,
      "end": 375.223,
      "dur": 2.453,
      "text": "There are three explanations."
    },
    {
      "id": "S76b",
      "start": 375.223,
      "speech_end": 379.257,
      "end": 380.057,
      "dur": 4.834,
      "text": "Only one of them has court records. Keep an eye on which."
    },
    {
      "id": "S76c",
      "start": 380.057,
      "speech_end": 382.947,
      "end": 383.747,
      "dur": 3.69,
      "text": "The first is the one everybody already knows."
    },
    {
      "id": "S77",
      "start": 383.747,
      "speech_end": 385.957,
      "end": 386.757,
      "dur": 3.01,
      "text": "Windows was sold as a platform."
    },
    {
      "id": "S78",
      "start": 386.757,
      "speech_end": 393.717,
      "end": 394.517,
      "dur": 7.76,
      "text": "Microsoft did not want to own every application on your computer. They wanted to own the floor it all stood on."
    },
    {
      "id": "S79",
      "start": 394.517,
      "speech_end": 400.637,
      "end": 401.437,
      "dur": 6.92,
      "text": "Need a file manager? Somebody will build one. Need a disk tool? Somebody will build one."
    },
    {
      "id": "S80",
      "start": 401.437,
      "speech_end": 402.94,
      "end": 403.74,
      "dur": 2.303,
      "text": "And that worked spectacularly."
    },
    {
      "id": "S81",
      "start": 403.74,
      "speech_end": 409.81,
      "end": 412.21,
      "dur": 8.47,
      "text": "But on its own it explains nothing, because Apple sells a platform too, and Apple ships a screenshot tool."
    },
    {
      "id": "S82",
      "start": 412.21,
      "speech_end": 415.82,
      "end": 416.62,
      "dur": 4.41,
      "text": "So here is the second reason, and this one has court dates."
    },
    {
      "id": "S83",
      "start": 416.62,
      "speech_end": 421.28,
      "end": 422.08,
      "dur": 5.46,
      "text": "In 1998, the American government took Microsoft to court."
    },
    {
      "id": "S84",
      "start": 422.08,
      "speech_end": 424.19,
      "end": 424.99,
      "dur": 2.91,
      "text": "Not for writing a bad browser."
    },
    {
      "id": "S85",
      "start": 424.99,
      "speech_end": 426.57,
      "end": 428.77,
      "dur": 3.78,
      "text": "For putting it in Windows."
    },
    {
      "id": "S86",
      "start": 428.77,
      "speech_end": 431.63,
      "end": 432.43,
      "dur": 3.66,
      "text": "A judge ordered the company to be split in two."
    },
    {
      "id": "S86b",
      "start": 432.43,
      "speech_end": 437.17,
      "end": 437.97,
      "dur": 5.54,
      "text": "That order was thrown out on appeal, and the case settled in 2001."
    },
    {
      "id": "S86c",
      "start": 437.97,
      "speech_end": 444.72,
      "end": 447.32,
      "dur": 9.35,
      "text": "And the question underneath it, whether putting the browser in Windows was legal at all, was never actually answered."
    },
    {
      "id": "S87",
      "start": 447.32,
      "speech_end": 452.91,
      "end": 453.71,
      "dur": 6.39,
      "text": "Then in 2004, the European Commission fined them nearly half a billion euros."
    },
    {
      "id": "S88",
      "start": 453.71,
      "speech_end": 458.12,
      "end": 458.92,
      "dur": 5.21,
      "text": "And ordered them to ship a version of Windows with the media player taken out."
    },
    {
      "id": "S89",
      "start": 458.92,
      "speech_end": 460.73,
      "end": 461.53,
      "dur": 2.61,
      "text": "Look at that sentence again."
    },
    {
      "id": "S90",
      "start": 461.53,
      "speech_end": 465.69,
      "end": 468.29,
      "dur": 6.76,
      "text": "A regulator required Microsoft to remove a tool from Windows."
    },
    {
      "id": "S91",
      "start": 468.29,
      "speech_end": 470.48,
      "end": 471.28,
      "dur": 2.99,
      "text": "And this is not ancient history."
    },
    {
      "id": "S92",
      "start": 471.28,
      "speech_end": 479.8,
      "end": 480.6,
      "dur": 9.32,
      "text": "Starting in 2016, an antivirus company complained to regulators in Russia, then in Germany, then in Brussels."
    },
    {
      "id": "S93",
      "start": 480.6,
      "speech_end": 483.51,
      "end": 484.31,
      "dur": 3.71,
      "text": "Because Windows had started defending itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "S93b",
      "start": 484.31,
      "speech_end": 490.23,
      "end": 491.83,
      "dur": 7.52,
      "text": "They withdrew the complaints in 2017, once Microsoft agreed to change how it behaved."
    },
    {
      "id": "S94",
      "start": 491.83,
      "speech_end": 494.12,
      "end": 494.92,
      "dur": 3.09,
      "text": "So put yourself in that meeting room."
    },
    {
      "id": "S95",
      "start": 494.92,
      "speech_end": 500.58,
      "end": 501.38,
      "dur": 6.46,
      "text": "Somebody proposes shipping the best archive tool on the market, for free, to a billion machines."
    },
    {
      "id": "S96",
      "start": 501.38,
      "speech_end": 503.74,
      "end": 504.54,
      "dur": 3.16,
      "text": "There is a market for archive tools."
    },
    {
      "id": "S97",
      "start": 504.54,
      "speech_end": 509.06,
      "end": 511.86,
      "dur": 7.32,
      "text": "Shipping the best possible tool is the most expensive thing Microsoft can do."
    },
    {
      "id": "S97b",
      "start": 511.86,
      "speech_end": 518.15,
      "end": 518.95,
      "dur": 7.09,
      "text": "And only for Microsoft. A smaller company could ship exactly the same tool and be fine."
    },
    {
      "id": "S97c",
      "start": 518.95,
      "speech_end": 530.43,
      "end": 531.23,
      "dur": 12.28,
      "text": "Once you are dominant, competition law limits how you can use that position. And replacing the very companies that built their business on your platform can start to look a lot like abusing it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S97d",
      "start": 531.23,
      "speech_end": 534.09,
      "end": 534.89,
      "dur": 3.66,
      "text": "Microsoft was trapped by its own success."
    },
    {
      "id": "S98",
      "start": 534.89,
      "speech_end": 537.45,
      "end": 538.25,
      "dur": 3.36,
      "text": "And the third reason is the quietest one."
    },
    {
      "id": "S99",
      "start": 538.25,
      "speech_end": 542.39,
      "end": 543.19,
      "dur": 4.94,
      "text": "Putting something in Windows means supporting it for the next twenty years."
    },
    {
      "id": "S100",
      "start": 543.19,
      "speech_end": 549.79,
      "end": 550.59,
      "dur": 7.4,
      "text": "It has to keep working. It can never be removed. It becomes somebody's whole workflow by Thursday."
    },
    {
      "id": "S101",
      "start": 550.59,
      "speech_end": 555.0,
      "end": 555.8,
      "dur": 5.21,
      "text": "Which is why, in 1996, Microsoft did something revealing."
    },
    {
      "id": "S102",
      "start": 555.8,
      "speech_end": 559.64,
      "end": 560.44,
      "dur": 4.64,
      "text": "They released a set of their own Windows utilities called PowerToys."
    },
    {
      "id": "S103",
      "start": 560.44,
      "speech_end": 566.33,
      "end": 567.13,
      "dur": 6.69,
      "text": "Written by Microsoft engineers. Downloaded separately. And officially unsupported."
    },
    {
      "id": "S104",
      "start": 567.13,
      "speech_end": 570.95,
      "end": 573.55,
      "dur": 6.421,
      "text": "We made these. They're good. We are not putting them in the box."
    },
    {
      "id": "S105",
      "start": 573.55,
      "speech_end": 576.71,
      "end": 577.51,
      "dur": 3.96,
      "text": "And that same rule explains the biggest gap of all."
    },
    {
      "id": "S106",
      "start": 577.51,
      "speech_end": 584.07,
      "end": 584.87,
      "dur": 7.36,
      "text": "Twenty programs. Twenty updaters. One checks at startup. One installs a service."
    },
    {
      "id": "S107",
      "start": 584.87,
      "speech_end": 589.97,
      "end": 590.77,
      "dur": 5.9,
      "text": "You log in on a Monday and six of them want your attention before you have opened anything."
    },
    {
      "id": "S108",
      "start": 590.77,
      "speech_end": 595.56,
      "end": 596.36,
      "dur": 5.59,
      "text": "Linux solved this decades ago. One command updates everything."
    },
    {
      "id": "S109",
      "start": 596.36,
      "speech_end": 597.663,
      "end": 598.463,
      "dur": 2.103,
      "text": "So why couldn't Windows?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S110",
      "start": 598.463,
      "speech_end": 601.773,
      "end": 602.573,
      "dur": 4.11,
      "text": "Because that command works for a reason people forget."
    },
    {
      "id": "S111",
      "start": 602.573,
      "speech_end": 609.523,
      "end": 610.323,
      "dur": 7.75,
      "text": "A Linux distribution builds the software itself. It compiles it, packages it, and knows what is in it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S112",
      "start": 610.323,
      "speech_end": 612.783,
      "end": 613.583,
      "dur": 3.26,
      "text": "Microsoft does not build your software."
    },
    {
      "id": "S113",
      "start": 613.583,
      "speech_end": 619.123,
      "end": 619.923,
      "dur": 6.34,
      "text": "Windows is not a distribution. It is a floor that anyone may put anything on."
    },
    {
      "id": "S114",
      "start": 619.923,
      "speech_end": 624.083,
      "end": 624.883,
      "dur": 4.96,
      "text": "Which is exactly why that installer-watching program existed."
    },
    {
      "id": "S115",
      "start": 624.883,
      "speech_end": 627.473,
      "end": 630.273,
      "dur": 5.39,
      "text": "Nobody had the list. Not even Windows."
    },
    {
      "id": "S116",
      "start": 630.273,
      "speech_end": 635.963,
      "end": 638.363,
      "dur": 8.09,
      "text": "So that is the answer. Platform, lawsuits, and the weight of anything you put in the box."
    },
    {
      "id": "S117",
      "start": 638.363,
      "speech_end": 640.243,
      "end": 641.843,
      "dur": 3.48,
      "text": "Except something has changed."
    },
    {
      "id": "S118",
      "start": 641.843,
      "speech_end": 644.403,
      "end": 645.203,
      "dur": 3.36,
      "text": "Because Windows now has a package manager."
    },
    {
      "id": "S119",
      "start": 645.203,
      "speech_end": 650.113,
      "end": 650.913,
      "dur": 5.71,
      "text": "It arrived in 2021. One command, and your programs update."
    },
    {
      "id": "S120",
      "start": 650.913,
      "speech_end": 658.613,
      "end": 659.413,
      "dur": 8.5,
      "text": "Windows has a proper terminal now. It runs Linux. PowerToys came back in 2019, open source."
    },
    {
      "id": "S121",
      "start": 659.413,
      "speech_end": 660.445,
      "end": 661.245,
      "dur": 1.833,
      "text": "So why now?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S122",
      "start": 661.245,
      "speech_end": 664.335,
      "end": 665.135,
      "dur": 3.89,
      "text": "Partly because the thing being protected has moved."
    },
    {
      "id": "S123",
      "start": 665.135,
      "speech_end": 668.399,
      "end": 669.199,
      "dur": 4.064,
      "text": "Windows is not where Microsoft makes its money any more."
    },
    {
      "id": "S123b",
      "start": 669.199,
      "speech_end": 672.739,
      "end": 673.539,
      "dur": 4.34,
      "text": "It now sits in the smallest of the company's three divisions."
    },
    {
      "id": "S123c",
      "start": 673.539,
      "speech_end": 679.379,
      "end": 680.179,
      "dur": 6.64,
      "text": "That division brings in less than a fifth of the revenue. It also contains the Xbox."
    },
    {
      "id": "S124",
      "start": 680.179,
      "speech_end": 683.189,
      "end": 683.989,
      "dur": 3.81,
      "text": "And nobody is going to court over a screenshot tool."
    },
    {
      "id": "S125",
      "start": 683.989,
      "speech_end": 688.235,
      "end": 689.035,
      "dur": 5.045,
      "text": "The fight moved to browsers, then to phones, then to the data centre."
    },
    {
      "id": "S126",
      "start": 689.035,
      "speech_end": 692.195,
      "end": 693.795,
      "dur": 4.76,
      "text": "The desktop is no longer the thing being defended."
    },
    {
      "id": "S127",
      "start": 693.795,
      "speech_end": 695.774,
      "end": 696.574,
      "dur": 2.78,
      "text": "But look closely at what shipped."
    },
    {
      "id": "S128",
      "start": 696.574,
      "speech_end": 704.344,
      "end": 705.144,
      "dur": 8.57,
      "text": "PowerToys, you download yourself. Process Explorer, you download yourself. Sysinternals, you download yourself."
    },
    {
      "id": "S129",
      "start": 705.144,
      "speech_end": 710.524,
      "end": 713.524,
      "dur": 8.38,
      "text": "Thirty years later, Microsoft still keeps its best tools one step outside Windows."
    },
    {
      "id": "S130",
      "start": 713.524,
      "speech_end": 715.635,
      "end": 716.434,
      "dur": 2.91,
      "text": "So the strange result stands."
    },
    {
      "id": "S131",
      "start": 716.434,
      "speech_end": 721.844,
      "end": 722.644,
      "dur": 6.21,
      "text": "Microsoft built a platform so successful that other people built everything missing from it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S132",
      "start": 722.644,
      "speech_end": 729.684,
      "end": 730.484,
      "dur": 7.84,
      "text": "And because those tools existed, Microsoft never had to. And for years, doing too much carried legal risk."
    },
    {
      "id": "S132b",
      "start": 730.485,
      "speech_end": 735.675,
      "end": 738.075,
      "dur": 7.59,
      "text": "Windows turned out to be extraordinarily good at hosting the tools it never shipped itself."
    },
    {
      "id": "S133",
      "start": 738.075,
      "speech_end": 747.065,
      "end": 747.865,
      "dur": 9.79,
      "text": "The user paid for that in complexity. A better file manager. A better search. Every one of them updating separately."
    },
    {
      "id": "S134",
      "start": 747.865,
      "speech_end": 752.455,
      "end": 753.255,
      "dur": 5.39,
      "text": "Which means the real Windows experience was never install it and you're done."
    },
    {
      "id": "S135",
      "start": 753.255,
      "speech_end": 754.902,
      "end": 755.702,
      "dur": 2.447,
      "text": "It was: install Windows."
    },
    {
      "id": "S136",
      "start": 755.702,
      "speech_end": 759.012,
      "end": 759.812,
      "dur": 4.11,
      "text": "Then build your own operating environment around it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S137",
      "start": 759.812,
      "speech_end": 763.072,
      "end": 763.872,
      "dur": 4.06,
      "text": "And the strangest part isn't that Microsoft couldn't do it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S138",
      "start": 763.872,
      "speech_end": 769.222,
      "end": 770.422,
      "dur": 6.55,
      "text": "It's that for twenty years, being brilliant at this was the one thing Windows could not afford to be."
    }
  ]
}